From: mklab <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] arch/amd64/builtin.c never declared the array its own comment describes

arch/amd64/builtin.c has said "wrap an array around the hex'ed dictionary file"
since 2003 and never wrapped it: static-dict.h is only the initializer DATA,
and the `static ucell forth_dictionary[...] = { #include ... };` declaration
lives in arch/x86/builtin.c. This file referenced forth_dictionary without ever
declaring it, so it could not compile at all -- invisible for 23 years because
nothing ever built arch/amd64.

Also sets dict_end/dict_last/dict_limit, the three sys_info fields the x86
revival (patch 01) had to add before load_dictionary worked there.

Arch-tested: amd64

diff --git a/arch/amd64/builtin.c b/arch/amd64/builtin.c
--- a/arch/amd64/builtin.c
+++ b/arch/amd64/builtin.c
@@ -14,12 +14,25 @@
  * wrap an array around the hex'ed dictionary file
  */
 
+/* SPIKE: the array this file's own comment says it wraps. Upstream never wrote it
+ * -- static-dict.h is only the initializer DATA, and arch/x86/builtin.c is where
+ * the declaration lives. Nothing ever compiled arch/amd64, so a file that cannot
+ * possibly build sat here since 2003 with a comment describing what it does not do. */
+#define DICTIONARY_SIZE (1024 * 1024 / sizeof(ucell))
+#define DICTIONARY_BASE ((ucell)((char *)&forth_dictionary))
+
+static ucell forth_dictionary[DICTIONARY_SIZE] = {
 #include "static-dict.h"
+};
 
 void collect_multiboot_info(struct sys_info *info);
 void collect_multiboot_info(struct sys_info *info)
 {
 	info->dict_start=(unsigned long *)forth_dictionary;
-	info->dict_end=(unsigned long *)((ucell)forth_dictionary +
-			sizeof(forth_dictionary));
+	/* dict_end/dict_last/dict_limit as arch/x86 sets them: the same three
+	 * fields patch 01 had to add there for load_dictionary to work at all. */
+	info->dict_end = (unsigned long *)FORTH_DICTIONARY_END;
+	info->dict_last = (ucell *)((unsigned char *)forth_dictionary +
+					    FORTH_DICTIONARY_LAST);
+	info->dict_limit = sizeof(forth_dictionary);
 }
